      "id": 1,
      "text": "Rolesville was incorporated on January 18, 1837, making it the second oldest town in Wake County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolesville%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town is named after William Roles, who purchased land and settled there, prompting the 1837 charter.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolesville%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Rolesville once thrived on agriculture and tobacco on large family‑owned tracts, a heritage that still shapes its greenway trails.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.rolesvillenc.gov/residents-visitors",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Little House Museum & Gallery, housed in a historic home, offers a glimpse into Rolesville’s past.",
